{
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-wanderer": "Wanderer",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-wanderer": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>No calling but the road, no burden but your paws.</i></font><br><br>Wanderers are flexible animal survivors with no special class strengths and no class weaknesses. They begin with fitted fangs and fitted claws.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-hunter": "Hunter",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-hunter": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>The trail ends where your teeth begin.</i></font><br><br>Hunters specialize in stalking prey, taking clean kills, and working carcasses. They are less suited to long mining work.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-stalker": "Stalker",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-stalker": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>Quiet breath, soft steps, sudden violence.</i></font><br><br>Stalkers are stealthy close-range ambushers. They move quietly, draw less attention, and bite harder, but they are frailer and poor miners.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-brute": "Brute",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-brute": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>A direct answer to most questions.</i></font><br><br>Brutes lean into close-range fighting and armor endurance. They are stronger and tougher, but louder and hungrier.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-guardian": "Guardian",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-guardian": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>Some bodies are built to outlast the problem.</i></font><br><br>Guardians are durable armored survivors. They take punishment well and wear armor efficiently, but they are slower and need more food.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-runner": "Runner",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-runner": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>The horizon is a suggestion, not a limit.</i></font><br><br>Runners trade toughness and mining ability for speed, jumping, and safer landings.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-mountaineer": "Mountaineer",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-mountaineer": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>The cliff is only rude if you stop halfway.</i></font><br><br>Mountaineers are terrain travelers with better sprinting, climbing, landing, and warmth. They forage less efficiently.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-miner": "Miner",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-miner": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>Stone opens for those stubborn enough to ask twice.</i></font><br><br>Miners break ground faster and find more ore. They are sturdy, but worse at animal work.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-digger": "Digger",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-digger": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>A den is just a home you argued out of the dirt.</i></font><br><br>Diggers are earthworkers and practical terrain survivors. They mine and forage better and land well, but sprint and bite worse.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-forager": "Forager",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-forager": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>The wild leaves food for anyone patient enough to notice.</i></font><br><br>Foragers live well from wild plants and gathered food. They need less food overall, but are weaker hunters and fighters.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-fieldhand": "Fieldhand",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-fieldhand": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>A clever paw can make a field feed more than one mouth.</i></font><br><br>Fieldhands are plant-focused survivors with better wild crop finds and plant nutrition. They give up bite strength and animal loot.",
  "characterclass-animalica-animal-scavenger": "Scavenger",
  "characterdesc-animalica-animal-scavenger": "<font color=\"#99c9f9\"><i>Useful things have a smell if you know how to listen.</i></font><br><br>Scavengers find value in ruins, vessels, forage, and carcasses. They give up mining speed and some bite strength.",

